/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (One of the biggest challenges while developing Obatku was building the app using a multiplatform technology for both Android and iOS. I had to handle platform-specific behaviors such as notifications, background reminders, permissions, and local storage, since each platform works differently. Ensuring a consistent user experience and maintaining compatibility across both platforms were also key challenges during development.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (Obatku is a mobile application designed to help users manage their medication schedules more effectively, especially for people who often forget to take their medicines on time. The core feature of the application is a smart medicine reminder system that allows users to add their medications, configure reminder schedules, and receive timely notifications to ensure consistent medicine intake.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (The idea for developing Obatku came from a personal experience. I created this application to help my father manage his medicines more easily, as keeping track of multiple medications and schedules can often be challenging. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (To solve the multiplatform challenges in Obatku, I separated the shared business logic from platform-specific implementations. I reused common code for features such as medicine management, scheduling, and data handling, while implementing native-specific solutions for notifications, permissions, and background services on Android and iOS.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
